Google's current documentation says that if you don't upgrade, the Free Trial billing account closes when the trial ends or the trial credit is exhausted, and the associated resources are stopped.

About removing/cancelling GPay

You do not need to remove or cancel your GPay/payment method just to avoid charges during a genuine Google Cloud Free Trial. The important thing is do not upgrade the Cloud Billing account to Paid.

However, do not simply remove the payment method without checking your billing account status first. Your screenshot should be checked under:

Google Cloud Console → Billing → Overview

Look for:

Billing account type/status: Free trial

If it says Paid, that is different.

My recommendation

Before the 88 days end:

Check that you have not clicked Upgrade.
Delete or stop any resources you no longer need, such as deployed Agent Engine resources or storage resources.
Go to Billing and confirm the account status is Free trial.
If you want to completely stop the trial early, you can close the Free Trial billing account. Google states that closing the billing account stops billable services and prevents further charges.

So, based on the screenshot you showed: if you remain on the Free Trial and do not upgrade to Paid, Google Cloud should not automatically start charging you when the 88 days finish.
